    {
      "id": "s10",
      "short": "Recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "body": "• **SQL**: tables, joins and transactions — a safe default.\n• **Documents**: flexible, self-contained records that scale out.\n• **Key–value**: fastest and simplest, lookup by id only.\n• Choose per kind of data; many systems use **several**.\n• Specialists like **search** are copies fed from the source of truth.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Next up: **Indexes** — why the same query can take 2 seconds or 2 milliseconds."
      },
